# SH-S01: users log in through Registration, which issues the JWT. Until the class's shared app
# (SH-U01) passes that token to our pages, the console uses one fixed token from here:
#
#  A) A real Registration token (once REGISTRATION_SIGNING_KEY or REGISTRATION_PUBLIC_KEY is in the root .env):
#     log in with a test account on Registration's site/Swagger (POST /api/Login/authenticate) and paste
#     the "accessToken" here. It lasts 60 minutes.
#  B) A dev token, signed with the key the API already checks:
#       dotnet user-jwts create --project backend --role "emergency:Admin" --name "Demo Admin"
#
# Use an Admin/Manager token for the full demo (closing calls needs Admin or Responder, test weather needs Admin).
# The token is built into the app, so after changing it rebuild: docker compose up --build frontend
VITE_API_TOKEN=
